//==
// # Mesh vertex numbering: types
//
// The vertex set of a model mesh is a disjoint union: the model's vertices, the interior points of
// each edge's discretization, and the interior vertices of each face mesh. A site names one element
// of that union combinatorially; the numbering is a bijection from the sites onto the global vertex
// indices 0 to N - 1. Shared boundary vertices coincide because two faces that cite one edge sample
// cite one site, and one site has one index. No position is compared anywhere in this mechanism.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Sites
//  - The numbering

//==
// # Sites

// The combinatorial identity of a global mesh vertex: which cell of the model's decomposition it
// samples and which sample it is. ModelVertex is a model vertex itself. EdgeInterior is the Slot-th
// interior point of an edge's discretization, counted from zero in the edge's forward direction, so
// Slot k is discretization point k + 1 (point 0 is the start vertex). FaceInterior is the Slot-th
// face-interior vertex of the face's mesh, counted from zero in the face mesh's local vertex order
// over the local vertices whose provenance is OnFace (refinement points, synthetic seam and pole
// points). A site carries no parameter, uv, or position: those are attributes, not identity.
type MeshVertexSite
    implements IValue
    = ModelVertex(Vertex: BrepVertexIndex)
    | EdgeInterior(Edge: BrepEdgeIndex, Slot: Integer)
    | FaceInterior(Face: BrepFaceIndex, Slot: Integer);

//==
// # The numbering

// The global numbering of mesh vertices (fixed by VOCABULARY.md): model vertices first, in
// BrepVertexIndex order, so mesh vertex v is model vertex v; then the interior points of each edge,
// edge by edge; then the face-interior vertices of each face, face by face. EdgeInteriorStart and
// FaceInteriorStart are offset arrays in the CSR form of JaggedArray.Offsets: EdgeInteriorStart has
// one entry per model edge plus one, edge e owns the indices from EdgeInteriorStart[e] up to, not
// including, EdgeInteriorStart[e + 1], and its last entry is where face interiors begin.
// FaceInteriorStart has one entry per model face plus one, the same way, and its last entry is the
// vertex count. The starts are non-decreasing, not increasing: a straight edge discretized by its
// two vertices owns an empty run, and so does a planar face with no interior vertex.
type MeshVertexNumbering
    implements IValue
{
    ModelVertexCount: Integer;
    EdgeInteriorStart: Array<Integer>;
    FaceInteriorStart: Array<Integer>;
}
